In this lab, I have made a modification to the JuiceShop deployment manifest to have 3 replicas, i.e. three instances of this app should be available at all times
I want to have 3 replicas of the JuiceShop running after I run this deployment manifest (i.e. juice-shop-deployment.yaml)

I have also modified the kind config file (i.e. kind-example-config.yaml) so that when KinD spins up a new kubernetes cluster, this cluster will have two control planes nodes and three worker nodes.
In this lab, if everything is set up correctly, we can show draining of one control plane and the other control plane should take over. 
Similarly we can drain all the JuiceShop instance from different worker nodes to see how the cluster instantly spin new instances of JuiceShop.
